 [; ── ambient process basics are NEVER gated (env.md §7: standard streams,
    process identity, argv, CPU count, exit/abort "are intrinsic to the
    running process and are never gated", the §7 table's `(none)` row).
    These run under an explicit grant that DELIBERATELY omits `env` (here
    `read`), so a regression that re-gates them behind the `env` capability
    surfaces as CXER0271 instead of the expected value. Contrast env-001,
    which DOES require `env` for `var`. ── ]
 [case id=env-052-stdout-no-cap level=core gate=enforced grant='read'
  [tags env stdout std-stream uncapped]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/env']
[$env:stdout]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[std-stream name=stdout fd=1]
#]]
 ]

